WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:08.272
Ally turned to Flo. "What's a VIP?" she asked nervously.

2
00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:13.535
"It stands for Very Important Person," Flo said.

3
00:00:13.536 --> 00:00:18.007
"Oh!" Ally sighed in relief.

4
00:00:18.008 --> 00:00:23.572
"In this case, it refers to the president of the National League of Rocket Scientists," Ray said.

5
00:00:23.573 --> 00:00:28.972
"The local league has been trying to get him to come to their gala for years, but he always turns them down.

6
00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:33.771
But when he heard it was going to be here at the diner, he changed his mind."

7
00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:38.151
"That's a big compliment to you, Ray," Flo said.

8
00:00:38.152 --> 00:00:40.759
"You think so?" Ray asked.

9
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:46.548
Flo nodded. "Your reputation is what's bringing him here."

10
00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:51.464
"But still, I think I should add some fancier dishes to the menu," Ray said.

11
00:00:51.465 --> 00:00:56.392
"I'd be happy to help you come up with some ideas," Flo said. Ray

12
00:00:56.393 --> 00:01:02.962
looked relieved. "Thanks, Flo. Well, I'd better get back to work." Ally

13
00:01:02.963 --> 00:01:06.512
and Flo returned to the dining room. "We

14
00:01:06.513 --> 00:01:11.620
should come up with an extra special dessert," Flo said. "Something

15
00:01:11.621 --> 00:01:15.077
to really impress the president." Randy

16
00:01:15.078 --> 00:01:17.191
stepped out of the kitchen. "I

17
00:01:17.192 --> 00:01:23.621
can bake a special cake. I've entered a few baking contests in my day." "You

18
00:01:23.622 --> 00:01:29.553
have?" Flo said. "I had no idea." Randy

19
00:01:29.554 --> 00:01:34.007
pulled out his phone and showed Ally and Flo photos of some of his cakes. There

20
00:01:34.008 --> 00:01:42.539
was a cake that looked like a turkey dinner, one that looked like a box of cereal, and even one that looked like a cell phone. "These

21
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:47.565
are amazing!" Ally exclaimed as she scrolled through the pictures. "I

22
00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:52.558
was thinking I could make a rocket ship cake for the gala," Randy said. "That

23
00:01:52.559 --> 00:01:58.285
would be perfect!" Flo said. ***

24
00:01:58.286 --> 00:02:03.287
Later Mateo came to plan the scavenger hunt with Ally.

25
00:02:03.288 --> 00:02:07.598
"The one my parents planned for me was cool," Ally said.

26
00:02:07.599 --> 00:02:13.778
"They hid clues everywhere—all over our ship, outside, and at a playground.

27
00:02:13.779 --> 00:02:18.671
The final prize was a day on the moon of Formaria for me and my friends.

28
00:02:18.672 --> 00:02:28.873
Formaria has just enough gravity to make it like a giant bouncy house. It was so much fun."

29
00:02:28.874 --> 00:02:33.525
"I wish I could take Bethany to Formaria," Mateo said.

30
00:02:33.526 --> 00:02:39.707
"Me too," Ally said. "What will you make the big final prize?"

31
00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:45.792
"A T-shirt from our favorite show, Cosmic Quest ," Mateo

32
00:02:45.793 --> 00:02:49.112
said. "I'm going to make all the gifts fit the theme of the show.

33
00:02:49.113 --> 00:02:55.040
And I can plant the clues here at the diner, the park, oh, and at one of the artist's sculptures.

34
00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:59.333
Now we just need to write some fun riddles for Bethany to solve."

35
00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:08.961
"Fun riddles?" Ally said. "I already have one! What's hotter than the moon but colder than Jupiter in winter?"

36
00:03:08.962 --> 00:03:13.353
Mateo shrugged. "I have no idea."

37
00:03:13.354 --> 00:03:19.814
"A galactic freezer!" Ally laughed.

38
00:03:19.815 --> 00:03:23.610
But to her surprise Mateo just looked confused.

39
00:03:23.611 --> 00:03:29.933
"Hmm," he said politely. "I'm not sure that riddle will work here on Earth.

40
00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:39.290
How about this one: Give me a tap and I'll give you some suds, I come in handy when you're covered in mud."

41
00:03:39.291 --> 00:03:44.951
Ally scratched her head. "A solar bath?"

42
00:03:44.952 --> 00:03:52.369
"No, silly." Mateo laughed. "Soap!"

43
00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:56.212
"I would never have guessed that." Ally grinned.

44
00:03:56.213 --> 00:04:00.703
"We can leave that clue on the soap dispenser in the ladies' restroom here."

45
00:04:00.704 --> 00:04:09.380
"Fantastic idea!"

46
00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:17.758
*** That evening Ray cooked a special dinner to welcome Ally to the

47
00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:21.617
house. "My famous enchiladas, just for you, Ally!" Ray

48
00:04:21.618 --> 00:04:29.048
said. "These look delicious, Ray. Thank you so much for letting me stay with you," Ally

49
00:04:29.049 --> 00:04:33.232
said. Ray smiled. "Like I told Mateo, I'd do anything

50
00:04:33.233 --> 00:04:40.816
for—" Just then Alpha squawked loudly. "The weather on Saturn is 280 degrees with fog and

51
00:04:40.817 --> 00:04:44.805
rain." Ally blushed as she pulled the device out of her pocket and sat on

52
00:04:44.806 --> 00:04:49.696
it. "Sorry about that! This silly device is acting

53
00:04:49.697 --> 00:04:54.048
up." "No problem," Ray said. "As I was saying, I'd do—"

54
00:04:54.049 --> 00:04:59.298
The device started playing loud music before quickly switching to an annoying beeping sound.

55
00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:04.435
While Ally was trying to get Alpha to be quiet, she saw Ray frown.

56
00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:12.939
"I'm so sorry, Ray!" Ally said. "I'll go put this thing away."

57
00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:18.400
She hurried upstairs. "You're still not working right, Alpha," she whispered.

58
00:05:18.401 --> 00:05:22.440
"I'd better put you back on the charger."

59
00:05:22.441 --> 00:05:26.839
As Ally stepped back into the dining room, she heard Ray talking to Mateo.

60
00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.207
"This house is usually so quiet, and now it's filled with noise."

61
00:05:31.208 --> 00:05:34.775
Ray shook his head. "What a change."

62
00:05:34.776 --> 00:05:38.477
"Oh no!" Ally thought, her heart skipping a beat.

63
00:05:38.478 --> 00:05:43.140
"An Astralian has the duty to always be a good and peaceful guest.

64
00:05:43.141 --> 00:05:54.806
Alpha and I are breaking that rule!"

